# Code Standards

Before editing files for any code change (feature, fix, refactor, or test update), read and follow `docs/CODE_STANDARDS.md`.

When standards conflict with ad-hoc preferences, **CODE_STANDARDS.md wins**.

## Required workflow

1. Read relevant sections of `docs/CODE_STANDARDS.md` before changing files.
2. For `lib/`, `src/` and `convex/` changes: read §9 and apply `@/lib/fp` patterns (see also `fp-paradigm.mdc`).
3. Apply standards while writing — not as a post-hoc cleanup.
4. Before finishing, verify against the **Code Review Checklist** at the bottom of the doc.

## Key areas (see doc for full detail)

- **Constants** — no magic numbers/strings; extract to constants files
- **Organization** — named exports, single responsibility, hooks for reusable logic
- **Types** — full TypeScript coverage; no `any` without justification
- **Docs** — JSDoc on public functions/hooks
- **Paradigm** — functional, declarative, immutable; use `lib/fp.ts` Result utilities
- **UI** — shadcn from `lib/components/ui/` (see also `shadcn-ui.mdc`)
- **Testing** — follow §12 when adding or updating tests

## Do not

- Skip the standards doc because the change seems small
- Introduce patterns that contradict documented conventions
- Mark work complete without checking the review checklist
